.*
.* Physical file constraints: WRKPFCST (the constraints a file name
.* selects, with change, remove and the records in check pending) and
.* EDTCPCST (the constraints in check pending, with the order they are
.* verified in). Geometry from the 7.1 captures
.* (verified/oracle71/audit/wrkpfcst, edtcpcst).
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=CSTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 15'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 11'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TYPECL BASETYPE='CHAR 9'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STATECL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=YNCL BASETYPE='CHAR 5'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SEQCL BASETYPE='CHAR 4'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 15'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SHORTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LIBCL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TIMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=CST CLASS=CSTCL.
:VAR NAME=FILE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=FILELIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=CSTTYPE CLASS=TYPECL.
:VAR NAME=CSTSTATE CLASS=STATECL.
:VAR NAME=CHKPND CLASS=YNCL.
:VAR NAME=SEQ CLASS=SEQCL.
:VAR NAME=CPSTS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=CPCST CLASS=SHORTCL.
:VAR NAME=CPFILE CLASS=LIBCL.
:VAR NAME=CPLIB CLASS=LIBCL.
:VAR NAME=VFYTIME CLASS=TIMECL.
:VAR NAME=ELAPSED CLASS=TIMECL.
:LISTDEF NAME=CSTS VARS='OPT CST FILE FILELIB CSTTYPE CSTSTATE CHKPND'.
:LISTDEF NAME=CPCSTS VARS='SEQ CPSTS CPCST CPFILE CPLIB VFYTIME ELAPSED'.
:KEYL NAME=WCKEYS HELP='KEYS/WCKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F15 ACTION='RETURN 15'.F15=Sort by
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.F22=Display constraint name
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=ECKEYS HELP='KEYS/ECKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display type
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='RETURN 13'.F13=Repeat all
:KEYI KEY=F15 ACTION='RETURN 15'.F15=Sort by
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKPFCST KEYL=WCKEYS HELP=WRKPFCST ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Physical File Constraints
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=CSTS ACTLEN=1.(No constraints to display)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGPFCST FILE(&FILELIB./&FILE.) CST(&CST.)' HELP='WRKPFCST/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD RMVPFCST FILE(&FILELIB./&FILE.) CST(&CST.)' HELP='WRKPFCST/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD DSPCPCST FILE(&FILELIB./&FILE.) CST(&CST.)' HELP='WRKPFCST/OPTIONS'.6=Display records in check pending
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKPFCST/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=CST USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=8 HELP='FLD/CST'.Constraint
:LISTCOL VAR=FILE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FILE'.File
:LISTCOL VAR=FILELIB USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FILELIB'.Library
:LISTCOL VAR=CSTTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CSTTYPE'.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=CSTSTATE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CSTSTATE'.State
:LISTCOL VAR=CHKPND USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CHKPND'.Check Pending
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 2, 4, 6 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=EDTCPCST KEYL=ECKEYS HELP=EDTCPCST ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=DATETIME BOTSEP=NONE.Edit Check Pending Constraints
:TOPINST.Type sequence, press Enter.
:TOPINST.Sequence:  1-99, *HLD
:TOPINST.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=CPCSTS.(No constraints to display)
:LISTCOL VAR=SEQ USAGE=INPUT HELP='FLD/SEQ'.Seq
:LISTCOL VAR=CPSTS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CPSTS'.Status
:LISTGRP COL=CSTGRP.----------Constraints-----------
:LISTCOL VAR=CPCST USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CST'.Cst
:LISTCOL VAR=CPFILE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FILE'.File
:LISTCOL VAR=CPLIB USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FILELIB'.Library
:ELISTGRP.
:LISTCOL VAR=VFYTIME USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/VFYTIME'.Verify Time
:LISTCOL VAR=ELAPSED USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/ELAPSED'.Elapsed Time
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKPFCST.Work with Physical File Constraints - Help
:P.The constraints of the files the name selects: unique and primary
keys, referential constraints and check constraints, with the state of
each. Option 2 enables or disables one, option 4 removes it, option 6
shows the records that keep it in check pending.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=EDTCPCST.Edit Check Pending Constraints - Help
:P.The constraints whose files hold records that break them. A file
with such a constraint cannot be used until the records are corrected
or the constraint is disabled. Give a constraint a sequence number to
have it verified again, lower numbers first; *HLD leaves it as it is.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WCKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F15=Sort by
:PD.Orders the list by another column.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Moves to the next entry that starts with what was last asked for.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Asks for a constraint name to move the list to.
:PT.F22=Display constraint name
:PD.Shows the whole name of the constraint the cursor is on, when it is
longer than the column.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/ECKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F11=Display type
:PD.Shows the type of each constraint in place of its status.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Repeat all
:PD.Gives every entry below the sequence number typed on the first.
:PT.F15=Sort by
:PD.Orders the list by another column.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Moves to the next entry that starts with what was last asked for.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Asks for a constraint name to move the list to.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPFCST/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to a constraint and press Enter.
The options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them
explains it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPFCST/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more constraints and press
Enter. The option runs for each constraint it is typed next to, in
order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Prompts the Change Physical File Constraint (CHGPFCST) command for
the constraint, to enable or disable it.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Runs the Remove Physical File Constraint (RMVPFCST) command for the
constraint.
:PT.6=Display records in check pending
:PD.Runs the Display Check Pending Constraint (DSPCPCST) command for the
constraint: the records that break it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CST'.Constraint
:P.The name of the constraint.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FILE'.File
:P.The physical file the constraint belongs to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FILELIB'.Library
:P.The library of the file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CSTTYPE'.Type
:P.*UNQCST for a unique constraint, *PRIKEY for a primary key, *REFCST
for a referential constraint, *CHKCST for a check constraint.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CSTSTATE'.State
:P.For a referential or check constraint: EST when it is established,
then ENB when it is enabled or DSB when it is disabled. Unique and
primary keys are always in force and show no state.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CHKPND'.Check pending
:P.YES when records of the file break the enabled constraint, so that
the file cannot be used until they are corrected; NO otherwise.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SEQ'.Sequence
:P.The order in which the constraint is verified again: 1 to 99, lower
numbers first. *HLD leaves the constraint in check pending.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CPSTS'.Status
:P.What is happening to the constraint: held, waiting to be verified,
being verified, or still in check pending after it was.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/VFYTIME'.Verify time
:P.How long verifying the constraint is expected to take.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ELAPSED'.Elapsed time
:P.How long the verification has run.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
